From e864d6c9838e0bfe52331439dddb110d5f6c3865 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:44:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] fix(fuji): 44px buttons and inputs, wrapping labels,
 token hover, one select style

From the Design System Agent's standalone audits of the pre-harness
pages (every area failed the same primitive rules):
- Button sm/md/lg and Input/Textarea are at least 44px tall
  (accessibility.minTouchTargetPx).
- Button labels wrap instead of overflowing at 320px with 200% text.
- Primary/utility hover darkens to --color-accent-deep (interaction
  states: active) instead of fading; secondary hover text is
  --color-accent-text, never mint.
- sm button text moves to the mono-12 step.
- selectClasses(): the NativeSelect pattern as a shared composer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0158uxufnvDxf4SMdnVi7Gjt
