From the Design System Agent's standalone audit, confirmed by its
screenshot tool:
- The header no longer scrolls sideways at 320px with 200% text:
  RoleBadge's built-in inline-flex overrode the caller's hidden, so it
  showed on phones; the right cluster can now shrink (min-w-0).
- Wordmark, nav links, Add pills and the chip's clear button are 44px;
  the wordmark link's name matches its text; landmarks are labelled.
- The header Admin/Questions link is secondary, so it never competes
  with a page's own primary action.
- The mobile menu is a labelled nav with a plain list of links (no
  role=menu without arrow keys), scrolls within the viewport, and shows
  the full email.
- Role badge, chip and bell counts move to the mono-12 step.
- Login: h1 gradient ends on --color-accent-text, the card uses
  --radius-lg, and the Google button is the Button primitive.

